  "data": {
    "accession": "PXD025662",
    "title": "Molecular architecture of the human tRNA ligase complex",
    "additionalAttributes": [],
    "projectDescription": "Chemical cross-linking coupled to mass spectrometry was used to study two tRNA ligase complexes, one consisting of subunits RTCB, DDX1, CGI-99, FAM98B and Ashwin (“full tRLC”) and one lacking Ashwin (“core tRLC”). Cross-linking was performed using the homobifunctional, noncleavable reagent, disuccinimidyl suberate (DSS).",
    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Chemical cross-linking was performed following previously described procedures (Leitner et al., Nat. Protoc., 2014). Samples were digested using endoproteinase Lys-C followed by trypsin. Digests were fractionated by size-exclusion chromatography and SEC fractions were analyzed by data-dependent LC-MS/MS on a Thermo Orbitrap Elite system. Additional experimental details are provided in the accompanying publication.",
    "dataProcessingProtocol": "MS/MS spectra were searched using xQuest (Walzthoeni et al., Nat. Methods, 2012), version 2.1.4, against the sequences of target proteins and identified contaminants.  Additional search settings were as follows: Enzyme = trypsin, maximum number of missed cleavages = 2, MS mass tolerances dependent on the respective data set, MS/MS mass tolerance = 0.2 Da for “common”-type fragment ions and 0.3 Da for “xlink”-type fragment ions. The scoring scheme from Walzthoeni et al., Nat. Methods, 2012, was used. Cross-linking identifications are compiled in spreadsheet files in Microsoft Excel format, with one tab per experimental replicate. A separate spreadsheet connects the raw files and the individual replicates.",
